From bf55f0799bcf18770931595ede92f6ce9941c84d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:47:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Noah-MP: apply the microphysics' frozen fraction to
 grid-scale precipitation only

With opt_snf 4 or 5, atm sets the snow fraction fpice = prcp_frozen/prcpnonc,
the microphysics' frozen fraction of grid-scale precipitation, and applies
it to all precipitation, convective included. Where the grid-scale
precipitation is only a trace of snow, fpice is 1 and the point's convective
rain falls as snow; where there is no grid-scale precipitation, convective
snow falls as rain.

Apply the microphysics fraction to grid-scale precipitation only, and make
convective precipitation snow below freezing. This is the host's own rule
for the snow fraction srflag (GFS_MP_generic_post, convective snow when
tsfc < 273.15 K, grid-scale phase from the microphysics); Noah-MP's atm
has the air temperature, not the skin temperature. The fresh-snow density
is blended by mass.

Rain + snow = prcp to one rounding step. Without convective precipitation
the result is bit-for-bit unchanged.

Compiled only: this branch's driver predates the single-column harness.
The change is line-for-line the one measured on the other branches (for
example GFS.v17: cold convective snow left 0.15 mm of snow over two days,
now 7.8 mm; without convective precipitation bit-for-bit unchanged). This
branch has opt_snf 4 only. Ported from the ufs/dev change.

Found while tracing a change in land evaporation: counting all
sedimentation out of Thompson's lowest layer as precipitation (a change
held separately) books a trace of the R1 placeholder as grid-scale snow,
which this rule turned into snow from convective rain.

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
---
 physics/module_sf_noahmplsm.f90 | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/physics/module_sf_noahmplsm.f90 b/physics/module_sf_noahmplsm.f90
index 4f9351f8..281493bf 100644
--- a/physics/module_sf_noahmplsm.f90
+++ b/physics/module_sf_noahmplsm.f90
@@ -992,6 +992,8 @@ contains
 
   real (kind=kind_phys)                                        :: pair   !atm bottom level pressure (pa)
   real (kind=kind_phys)                                        :: prcp_frozen   !total frozen precipitation [mm/s] ! mb/an : v3.7
+  real (kind=kind_phys)                                        :: fpcv          !frozen fraction of convective precipitation
+  real (kind=kind_phys)                                        :: bdfall0       !snow density before the mix [kg/m3]
   real (kind=kind_phys), parameter                             :: rho_grpl = 500.0  ! graupel bulk density [kg/m3] ! mb/an : v3.7
   real (kind=kind_phys), parameter                             :: rho_hail = 917.0  ! hail bulk density [kg/m3]    ! mb/an : v3.7
 ! --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -1071,6 +1073,7 @@ contains
 
      bdfall = min(120.,67.92+51.25*exp((sfctmp-tfrz)/2.59))       !mb/an: change to min  
      if(opt_snf == 4) then
+        bdfall0 = bdfall
         prcp_frozen = prcpsnow + prcpgrpl + prcphail
         if(prcpnonc > 0. .and. prcp_frozen > 0.) then
 	  fpice = min(1.0,prcp_frozen/prcpnonc)
@@ -1081,6 +1084,14 @@ contains
 	  fpice = 0.0
         endif
 	
+        ! the microphysics fraction is for grid-scale precipitation; convective precipitation is snow below freezing
+        if(prcpconv + prcpshcv > 0.) then
+          fpcv = 0.0
+          if(sfctmp < tfrz) fpcv = 1.0
+          if(opt_snf == 4 .and. fpcv > 0. .and. fpice > 0.) bdfall = (bdfall*fpice*prcpnonc + &
+                 bdfall0*(prcpconv + prcpshcv)) / (fpice*prcpnonc + prcpconv + prcpshcv)
+          fpice = fpice + (fpcv - fpice)*(prcpconv + prcpshcv)/prcp
+        end if
      endif
 
      rain   = prcp * (1.-fpice)
-- 
